kavis-share (1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * First cut of Kavis Share (item 76, decision 11): discovery over the
    LocalSend multicast announcement plus direct registration, and file
    transfer over its prepare-upload/upload pair — so a device asks
    before it sends and a stranger can only ask, once, and be refused.
  * Visibility is enforced where the announcement is made, not at the
    edges: "off" means nothing leaves this machine, because the
    announcement is the thing that tells a stranger a device is here.
  * Files land in ~/downloads/kavis-share and never outside it; the
    name the sender chose is stripped to its basename first, and an
    existing file is never overwritten.

 -- Karan <farukyildiz3207@gmail.com>  Mon, 08 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0300
